        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "For students near San Francisco’s 2.0 eighth-grade-GPA cutoff, taking ethnic studies increased ninth-grade credits earned by 23 credits.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The authors derive this local IV estimate from a 6.328 reduced-form credit discontinuity (robust SE 2.201; N=1,404) and the 0.273 take-up jump. The paper characterizes 23 credits as roughly four courses and notes that dropout reductions may contribute to the result.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
